# Testing strategy

The Definition of Done gate requires production-code changes to include a recognised test unless a time-bounded waiver exists in `.agent-standard/waivers.json`.

| Test type | Location | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
{% if language_stack == 'py-fastapi' -%}
| Unit | `tests/unit/test_*.py` | Domain and application behavior without I/O |
| Integration | `tests/integration/test_*.py` | FastAPI and adapter behavior across real boundaries |
{% elif language_stack == 'ts-next' -%}
| Unit/component | `__tests__/` or `*.test.ts(x)` | Synchronous logic and component behavior |
| End-to-end | `e2e/*.spec.ts` | App Router, async server behavior, and user-visible flows |
{% else -%}
| Unit | colocated `*.test.ts` or `tests/unit/` | Pure behavior without infrastructure |
| Integration | `tests/integration/` | Wired adapters and service boundaries |
{% endif %}

Tests must assert observable behavior. A test changed only to satisfy the filename gate is a review failure even if automation passes.
